WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:02.231
Hey, I'm Dale! This is Making with ML.

00:00:02.231 --> 00:00:04.318
Today, you'll build
a Machine Learning model

00:00:04.318 --> 00:00:06.979
right here, right now,
and in under ten minutes.

00:00:06.979 --> 00:00:09.475
I'll show how to use a tool
called Teachable Machines

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:12.079
to train a model
from your browser really fast.

00:00:12.079 --> 00:00:13.840
Let's get to it!

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.446
Today, I thought it'd be fun
to train a model

00:00:15.446 --> 00:00:17.841
that recognizes letters
that I make with my body,

00:00:17.841 --> 00:00:20.464
like A, B, C.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.082
But for starters,
I'll just train the model

00:00:23.082 --> 00:00:25.898
to recognize the letters Y, M, C, A.

00:00:25.898 --> 00:00:27.467
I'll use Teachable Machines to do this.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.405
It's one of the coolest ML tools out there

00:00:29.405 --> 00:00:33.210
because it allows you to train a model
that's for photos, audio, or a pose,

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.355
without writing any code
and it runs straight in your browser.

00:00:36.355 --> 00:00:39.198
All you need to get started
is a computer with a webcam.

00:00:39.198 --> 00:00:41.854
So first, go to
<i>teachablemachine.withgoogle.com</i>

00:00:41.854 --> 00:00:43.362
and click <i>Get Started.</i>

00:00:43.362 --> 00:00:45.339
From here, you'll see there are
three different models

00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:47.208
you can train in each audio and pose,

00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:49.215
but we'll make a "Pose" project.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.777
The idea with Machine Learning

00:00:50.777 --> 00:00:53.222
is to train a computer 
to find patterns in data.

00:00:53.222 --> 00:00:55.287
So step 1 is to collect training data.

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:57.897
In the UI, you can collect training data
right from your webcam,

00:00:57.897 --> 00:01:01.649
so I'll create a bunch of examples of me
making the letter Y with my body.

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:03.986
First, create a new <i>Class</i>
with whatever you want to detect--

00:01:03.986 --> 00:01:05.812
in this case, the letter Y.

00:01:06.919 --> 00:01:09.179
So, as you can see,
the UI's already detecting

00:01:09.179 --> 00:01:12.372
my pose and my facial expressions
using a pre-trained model,

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:15.964
but what I really want it to do 
is recognize the letters I'm making.

00:01:15.964 --> 00:01:18.037
Let's take some example pictures.

00:01:18.037 --> 00:01:19.229
Take pictures of yourself

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:21.759
from lots of different angles
and distances from the camera,

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:24.004
which will prevent the model
from overfitting on features

00:01:24.004 --> 00:01:26.067
about the room or the camera angles.

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:30.880
Now I'll collect some data
for M, C, and A.

00:01:31.775 --> 00:01:34.300
Once you've done collecting data,
click <i>Train Model.</i>

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.919
When you hit this button,
<i>TensorFlow.js</i> actually trains

00:01:36.919 --> 00:01:39.073
a new neural network from data
right in your browser,

00:01:39.073 --> 00:01:40.635
so do not close this window.

00:01:40.635 --> 00:01:42.708
Your computer is doing
a lot of work under the hood.

00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:45.836
Click <i>Advanced</i> and <i>Under the Hood</i>
to learn more how it works.

00:01:45.836 --> 00:01:47.233
Once your model's done training,

00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:49.318
you can try it out
right here in the browser.

00:01:49.318 --> 00:01:53.523
Tu-tu, tu-tu, tu-tu tu!
Hmm, hm-hm.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.098
It works!

00:01:55.098 --> 00:01:59.017
The best thing about Teachable Machines
is it's really easy to export your model.

00:01:59.017 --> 00:02:01.650
You can either download it
as a TensorFlow model file,

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.473
or you can have
Teachable Machines host it for you,

00:02:04.473 --> 00:02:06.979
and it'll even give you
this nice shareable link.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.126
Plus, there's a nice
JavaScript code sample

00:02:09.126 --> 00:02:12.151
that you can use to easily add
the model to your web app.

00:02:12.151 --> 00:02:15.037
To learn about my favorite
easy-to-use Machinery and tools,

00:02:15.037 --> 00:02:16.861
check out my blog below.

00:02:16.861 --> 00:02:17.729
That's it for now.

00:02:17.729 --> 00:02:18.909
If you liked what you saw today,

00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:21.305
tell me what you want me
to build in the comments.

00:02:21.305 --> 00:02:23.248
Until then, see you next time.

00:02:23.248 --> 00:02:25.025
♪ [music] ♪

